          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle Q_{2}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/b86e8bff64d5e62fc8f45a35875e78bc9bef74a9" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.893ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle Q_{2}}"/></span>along a path in one component <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt73" id="mwuQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X_1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X_{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>X</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X_{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f70b2694445a5901b24338a2e7a7e58f02a72a32" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.979ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X_{1}}"/></span> and comes back along a path in the other component <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt74" id="mwug" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X_2"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X_{2}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>X</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X_{2}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/2ad47c14b8a092f182512e76c96638aea6e3bea1" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.979ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X_{2}}"/></span>. This suggests that <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt75" id="mwuw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_1(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{1}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{1}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1daf37d45ddbb3999d6395aa6cd3b2275da6cbf1" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.775ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{1}(X)}"/></span> admits an increasing filtration</p>

<dl id="mwvA"><dd id="mwvQ"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt76" id="mwvg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" 0\\subset W_0\\subset W_1 \\subset W_2=H^1(X), "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle 0\subset W_{0}\subset W_{1}\subset W_{2}=H^{1}(X),}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mn>0</mn>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>W</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>0</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>W</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>W</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle 0\subset W_{0}\subset W_{1}\subset W_{2}=H^{1}(X),}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7922f360b1b0ccd6ad5fd21f0c03dbe56bc4f1a4" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:30.894ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle 0\subset W_{0}\subset W_{1}\subset W_{2}=H^{1}(X),}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwvw">whose successive quotients <i id="mwwA">W<sub id="mwwQ">n</sub></i>/<i id="mwwg">W</i><sub id="mwww"><i id="mwxA">n</i>−1</sub> originate from the cohomology of smooth complete varieties, hence admit (pure) Hodge structures, albeit of different weights. Further examples can be found in "A Naive Guide to Mixed Hodge Theory".<sup about="#mwt79" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwxQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwyQ" aria-labelledby="Definition_of_mixed_Hodge_structure"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Definition_of_mixed_Hodge_structure">Definition of mixed Hodge structure</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Definition of mixed Hodge structure"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwyg">A <b id="mwyw">mixed Hodge structure</b> on an abelian group <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt80" id="mwzA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_{\\Z}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Z} }}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Z} }}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/234b78b24e88ae30d843d3d7fcf2e24ff7d6702a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:3.26ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Z} }}"/></span> consists of a finite decreasing filtration <i id="mwzQ">F<sup id="mwzg">p</sup></i> on the complex vector space <i id="mwzw">H</i> (the complexification of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt81" id="mw0A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_{\\Z}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Z} }}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Z} }}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/234b78b24e88ae30d843d3d7fcf2e24ff7d6702a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:3.26ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Z} }}"/></span>), called the <b id="mw0Q">Hodge filtration</b> and a finite increasing filtration <i id="mw0g">W<sub id="mw0w">i</sub></i> on the rational vector space <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt82" id="mw1A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_{\\Q} = H_{\\Z} \\otimes_{\\Z} \\Q"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Q} }=H_{\mathbb {Z} }\otimes _{\mathbb {Z} }\mathbb {Q} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <msub>
          <mo>⊗<!-- ⊗ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Q} }=H_{\mathbb {Z} }\otimes _{\mathbb {Z} }\mathbb {Q} }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a4860b3d612846d395815190342d59a9763b8cfc" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:15.777ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Q} }=H_{\mathbb {Z} }\otimes _{\mathbb {Z} }\mathbb {Q} }"/></span> (obtained by extending the scalars to rational numbers), called the <b id="mw1Q">weight filtration</b>, subject to the requirement that the <i id="mw1g">n</i>-th associated graded quotient of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt83" id="mw1w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_{\\Q}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{\mathbb {Q} }}">
