    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}x_{0}^{2}x_{1}^{2},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{1}x_{2},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{1}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{2}^{2},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}^{2}x_{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}^{2}x_{3},\\x_{0}x_{1}x_{2}^{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}x_{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{2}^{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}x_{2}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{1}^{2}x_{2}^{2},&amp;x_{1}^{2}x_{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{1}^{2}x_{3}^{2},\\x_{1}x_{2}^{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{1}x_{2}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{2}^{2}x_{3}^{2}\end{array}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/34d9f04de700e3fdf9369c9d9819b22f2f248bea" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -4.505ex; width:79.398ex; height:10.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}x_{0}^{2}x_{1}^{2},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{1}x_{2},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{1}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{2}^{2},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}^{2}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}^{2}x_{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}^{2}x_{3},\\x_{0}x_{1}x_{2}^{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}x_{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}x_{1}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{0}x_{2}^{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{0}x_{2}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{1}^{2}x_{2}^{2},&amp;x_{1}^{2}x_{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{1}^{2}x_{3}^{2},\\x_{1}x_{2}^{2}x_{3},&amp;x_{1}x_{2}x_{3}^{2},&amp;x_{2}^{2}x_{3}^{2}\end{array}}}"/></span> which is 19-dimensional. There is an extra vector in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt127" id="mwAUo" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{1,1}(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{1,1}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{1,1}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c1c6aa1410b8dad766b7743eb2f65076017df4c9" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:8.226ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{1,1}(X)}"/></span> given by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lefschetz_manifold#Definitions" title="Lefschetz manifold" id="mwAUs">Lefschetz class</a> <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt128" id="mwAUw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"[L]"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle [L]}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mi>L</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle [L]}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c1eba88cad4b17de726ed2c779b29eecdf5819a2" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:2.877ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle [L]}"/></span>. From the Lefschetz hyperplane theorem and Hodge duality, the rest of the cohomology is in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt129" id="mwAU0" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{k,k}(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{k,k}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{k,k}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d655d630cdd60cd7c9035ebe119bd59877ae8715" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:8.295ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{k,k}(X)}"/></span> as is <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt130" id="mwAU4" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle 1}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mn>1</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle 1}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/92d98b82a3778f043108d4e20960a9193df57cbf" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.162ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle 1}"/></span>-dimensional. Hence the Hodge diamond reads <!--
--><table style="text-align:center;" about="#mwt111" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAU8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Hodge diamond\n","href":"./Template:Hodge_diamond"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1\n"},"2":{"wt":"0"},"3":{"wt":"0\n"},"4":{"wt":"1"},"5":{"wt":"20"},"6":{"wt":"1\n"},"7":{"wt":"0"},"8":{"wt":"0\n"},"9":{"wt":"1"}},"i":0}}]}'><tbody><tr><td></td><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">1</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">0</td><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">0</td><td></td></tr><tr><td style="width:2.5em;">1</td><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">20</td><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">1</td></tr><tr><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">0</td><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">0</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td style="width:2.5em;">1</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></li>
<li id="mwAVA">We can also use the previous isomorphism to verify the genus of a degree <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt131" id="mwAVE" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"d"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle d}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>d</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle d}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/e85ff03cbe0c7341af6b982e47e9f90d235c66ab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.216ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle d}"/></span> plane curve. Since <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt132" id="mwAVI" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"x^d + y^d + z^d"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle x^{d}+y^{d}+z^{d}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>x</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>d</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>y</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>d</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>z</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>d</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle x^{d}+y^{d}+z^{d}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ac3c826b10a3aaa201efe98159d6258ea575fc83" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:12.537ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle x^{d}+y^{d}+z^{d}}"/></span> is a smooth curve and the Ehresmann fibration theorem guarantees that every other smooth curve of genus <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt133" id="mwAVM" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"g"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle g}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>g</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle g}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d3556280e66fe2c0d0140df20935a6f057381d77" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:1.116ex; height:2.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle g}"/></span> is diffeomorphic, we have that the genus then the same. So, using the isomorphism of primitive cohomology with the graded part of the Jacobian ring, we see that <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt134" id="mwAVQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{1,0} \\cong R(f)_{d-3} \\cong \\Complex [x,y,z]_{d-3}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{1,0}\cong R(f)_{d-3}\cong \mathbb {C} [x,y,z]_{d-3}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mn>0</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>≅<!-- ≅ --></mo>
        <mi>R</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>f</mi>
        <msub>
          <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>d</mi>
            <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
            <mn>3</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>≅<!-- ≅ --></mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">C</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mi>x</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>y</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>z</mi>
        <msub>
          <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>d</mi>
            <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
            <mn>3</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{1,0}\cong R(f)_{d-3}\cong \mathbb {C} [x,y,z]_{d-3}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/0a2474f7cfc5e78ae8e24d479d74c231906faef4" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:30.484ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{1,0}\cong R(f)_{d-3}\cong \mathbb {C} [x,y,z]_{d-3}}"/></span> This implies that the dimension is <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt135" id="mwAVU" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":" {2 + d - 3 \\choose 2} = {d-1 \\choose 2} = \\frac{(d-1)(d-2)}{2}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle {2+d-3 \choose 2}={d-1 \choose 2}={\frac {(d-1)(d-2)}{2}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow>
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-OPEN">
              <mo maxsize="2.047em" minsize="2.047em">(</mo>
            </mrow>
